# ========================================
# STRAVA API CREDENTIALS
# ========================================
# 
# This template shows the required environment variables for Strava integration.
# 
# SETUP INSTRUCTIONS:
# 1. Copy this file to ".env" (create a new file named .env)
# 2. Go to https://www.strava.com/settings/api
# 3. Create a new application to get your credentials
# 4. Fill in your actual values below (replace the placeholder text)
# 5. NEVER commit the .env file to git (it's in .gitignore)
#
# ========================================

# Required: Strava Application ID
# Find this on your Strava API application page after creating an app
CLIENT_ID=218481

# Required: Strava Application Secret
# This is the "Client Secret" shown on your Strava API application page
CLIENT_SECRET=ba4363b2285411bb09637e6a3917c04a952240a1

# Required: Access Token
# Generated after OAuth authorization (run setup_strava_auth.py first time)
ACCESS_TOKEN=7a18fb1ed24c3feb35808556da7ba682771f4ac1

# Required: Refresh Token  
# Used to get new access tokens when they expire
# Generated after OAuth authorization (run setup_strava_auth.py first time)
REFRESH_TOKEN=d893a5c5cd5e190b6b122534a066838a9cbaa470

# ========================================
# HOW TO GET CREDENTIALS:
# ========================================
#
# STEP 1: Create a Strava API Application
# ----------------------------------------
# 1. Go to: https://www.strava.com/settings/api
# 2. Click "Create an App" or "My API Application"
# 3. Fill in the form:
#    - Application Name: "Training Plan Tracker" (or your choice)
#    - Category: Choose appropriate category
#    - Club: Leave blank unless applicable
#    - Website: http://localhost (for personal use)
#    - Authorization Callback Domain: localhost
# 4. Click "Create"
# 5. You'll see your CLIENT_ID and CLIENT_SECRET
#
# STEP 2: Copy CLIENT_ID and CLIENT_SECRET
# -----------------------------------------
# 1. Copy this .env.template file to .env
# 2. Replace "your_client_id_here" with your actual Client ID (number)
# 3. Replace "your_client_secret_here" with your actual Client Secret (hex string)
#
# STEP 3: Get ACCESS_TOKEN and REFRESH_TOKEN
# -------------------------------------------
# 1. Run: python setup_strava_auth.py
# 2. Your browser will open to Strava authorization page
# 3. Click "Authorize" to allow access to your activities
# 4. Copy the authorization code from the URL
# 5. Paste it when prompted in the script
# 6. The script will automatically update your .env file with tokens
#
# STEP 4: Verify Setup
# ---------------------
# 1. Run: python sync_strava_to_excel.py
# 2. If successful, you'll see your Strava activities fetched
# 3. Your workbook will be updated with activity data
#
# ========================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING:
# ========================================
#
# ERROR: "Invalid client_id"
# - Double-check CLIENT_ID value matches Strava API page exactly
#
# ERROR: "Invalid client_secret"  
# - Double-check CLIENT_SECRET value matches Strava API page exactly
#
# ERROR: "Unauthorized" or "Token expired"
# - Run setup_strava_auth.py again to refresh tokens
# - Access tokens expire after 6 hours, refresh tokens are long-lived
#
# ERROR: "Rate limit exceeded"
# - Strava API has rate limits (200 requests per 15 mins, 2000 per day)
# - Wait 15 minutes and try again
# - Sync less frequently (once per week recommended)
#
# ========================================
# SECURITY NOTES:
# ========================================
#
# - NEVER share your .env file or commit it to git
# - The .gitignore file should include .env to prevent accidental commits
# - CLIENT_SECRET and tokens give full access to your Strava account
# - If tokens are compromised, regenerate them at https://www.strava.com/settings/api
# - You can revoke application access anytime in Strava settings
#
# ========================================
# API SCOPES:
# ========================================
#
# This application requests the following Strava scopes:
# - read: Read public profile information
# - activity:read_all: Read all activity data (including private activities)
#
# If you need to modify activities (not currently implemented), you would need:
# - activity:write: Create/update/delete activities
#
# ========================================
